        <!-- CHALLENGE -->
        <section class="project-section">

            <div class="section-number">01</div>

            <div class="section-content">

                <h2>CHALLENGE</h2>

                <p>
                    
                    <em>
                        How might we make Hero Imaging's complex medical image analysis software easier to understand, learn and navigate?
                    </em>
                </p>
                
                <p>
                    Hero Imaging had developed a powerful node-based tool for medical image analysis, but the existing interface had evolved without a clear set of design principles. This made it difficult to communicate system states, errors and warnings clearly.
                </p>
                
                <p>
                    Our task was to investigate the existing experience and develop a more intuitive visual language without changing the underlying functionality.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>

        <section class="project-section">

            <div class="section-number">02</div>

            <div class="section-content">

                <h2>RESEARCH</h2>

                <p>
                    Before redesigning the interface, we needed to understand both the product and its users.
We started by learning the existing Hero software ourselves and analysing similar tools. We then conducted interviews and surveys with people who had experience using Hero and comparable software.
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    The research revealed five main areas for improvement:
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    Nodes · Micronodes · Colour system · Notes · Settings
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    These areas became the foundation for the following design iterations.

                   
                </p>

               

            </div>

        </section>

        <section class="project-section">

            <div class="section-number">03</div>

            <div class="section-content">

                <h2>DESIGN PROCESS</h2>

                <p>
                    Design: We began with low-fidelity sketches on paper and whiteboards. This allowed us to quickly explore different solutions before committing to detailed visual design.
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    Prototype: Promising concepts were developed into high-fidelity prototypes in Figma. We created multiple variations of redesigned components and tested different approaches to colour, icons, hierarchy and interaction.
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    Feedback: The designs were reviewed both internally and with Hero Imaging. Feedback from the company was incorporated into subsequent iterations.
                </p>
                
                    

            </div>

        </section>





