        <section class="project-section">

            <div class="section-number">05</div>

            <div class="section-content">

                <h2>Testing</h2>

                <p>
                    To evaluate the redesign, we conducted an A/B survey comparing Hero's original interface with our redesigned version.
                    The survey contained 35 questions covering the redesigned nodes, colour system, icons, error handling, warnings,
                    micronodes, workflows, notes and settings. Nine experienced Hero users were invited and five completed the survey.

                    <br>
                    <br>
                    The positive feedback we got were that they thought the nodes were clearer, improved error and warning handling,
                    more useful notes functionality and improved settings navigation. Users also identified areas that still needed refinement,
                     including overly strong colours and ways to communicate when a node had finished running.
                     After the feedback we changed two colours, added icons and created a green outline to show that a node has been active. 

                    <br>
    
                
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>

        <section class="project-section final-section">

            <div class="section-number">06</div>

            <div class="section-content">

                <h2>Outcome</h2>

                <p>
                    The final outcome was a redesigned interface concept for Hero Imaging, addressing several of the usability issues identified during the research phase.
                    The redesign introduced clearer visual states, improved error and warning communication, a refined colour system, more intuitive icons, an updated Notes experience and a more accessible settings interface.
                    While the project did not include implementation, the final design was grounded in user research, iterative prototyping and feedback from experienced Hero users.
    
                
                </p>

            </div>



